        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "e5793d4e-9051-37cc-b024-f94bc26870c1",
                "word": "cousinship",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "0130b781-3eae-4541-bfe5-06153b5c9b42",
                        "entry_id": "e5793d4e-9051-37cc-b024-f94bc26870c1",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "cousinships"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5a9a5930-908f-3d0a-9e6d-d97b93399431",
                        "entry_id": "e5793d4e-9051-37cc-b024-f94bc26870c1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The state of being cousins, or the relationship that exists among cousins."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c9c42264-b1f0-4570-8cce-2a818ead80b1",
                                "sense_id": "5a9a5930-908f-3d0a-9e6d-d97b93399431",
                                "text": "“How long did you reside with him and his sisters after the cousinship was discovered?”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f2debddf-3057-480c-861a-7a680cf6946d",
                                "sense_id": "5a9a5930-908f-3d0a-9e6d-d97b93399431",
                                "text": "His creed of determinism was such that it almost amounted to a vice, and quite amounted, on its negative side, to a renunciative philosophy which had cousinship with that of Schopenhauer and Leopardi."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ebe74dd-3a2b-4d5e-b945-b6e6cf1dcb0d",
                                "sense_id": "5a9a5930-908f-3d0a-9e6d-d97b93399431",
                                "text": "What he repudiated was cousinship with the ape, and the implied suspicion of a rudimentary tail, because it was offensive to his sense of his own dignity, and because he thought that apes were ridiculous, and tails diabolical when associated with the erect posture."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "90f76c9a-28ac-4210-a9ad-b75b33e15810",
                                "sense_id": "5a9a5930-908f-3d0a-9e6d-d97b93399431",
                                "text": "He describes a beautiful thought experiment to demonstrate a rabbit’s cousinship to a leopard."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "88d5b478-e069-4031-8b99-e5deacbdd3d4",
                        "source_entry_id": "e5793d4e-9051-37cc-b024-f94bc26870c1",
                        "source_sense_id": "5a9a5930-908f-3d0a-9e6d-d97b93399431",
                        "source_sense_description": "state of being cousins",
                        "target_lang_word": "cousinage",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cousinage",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fe2120ed-8ac7-3306-9578-0ddb7891f8d4",
                                        "entry_id": "62a8932e-8d08-37f2-b9d3-c1e9246a018e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Parenté qui existe entre cousins."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d6da6f3-6d73-4bcd-a187-a2f48877f1fd",
                                                "sense_id": "fe2120ed-8ac7-3306-9578-0ddb7891f8d4",
                                                "text": "La plupart des patronymes se répétaient et se ressemblaient, à croire que ces gens vivaient tous en cousinage. Mais ce n'était qu'un faux-semblant, le postier de Péronville l'avait bien avertie là-dessus. Elle l'entendait encore lui dire :« Ne te trompe surtout pas de destinataires, ma fille, quand tu liras tes enveloppes ! »"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ed4285e8-5a9a-314e-b70e-5411fc565416",
                                        "entry_id": "62a8932e-8d08-37f2-b9d3-c1e9246a018e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Tout l’ensemble des parents."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51386bc0-e0b9-4023-94bd-45ddb6cb4288",
                                                "sense_id": "ed4285e8-5a9a-314e-b70e-5411fc565416",
                                                "text": "On aurait prévenu le cousinage, on aurait mis du buis dans un vase d’eau bénite, et des chandelles, et un chapelet…"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a911e247-c61c-4f22-8747-dc940e10d5b4",
                                                "sense_id": "ed4285e8-5a9a-314e-b70e-5411fc565416",
                                                "text": "Par ailleurs, c’était par l’alliance matrimoniale que se reproduisait la cohésion des « cousinages » (les gentes, conçues comme des parentèles issues d’un ancêtre commun – mythique et éponyme – et qui servaient de cadres de mobilisation dans la lutte pour le pouvoir)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "68d8267d-e122-3abe-9ee4-73cb77a067b0",
                                        "entry_id": "62a8932e-8d08-37f2-b9d3-c1e9246a018e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relation d’analogie, de ressemblance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "176b6860-6807-4787-a48b-6b5cabb535bc",
                                                "sense_id": "68d8267d-e122-3abe-9ee4-73cb77a067b0",
                                                "text": "La grande objection et imputation faite aux Jansénistes était toujours leur cousinage avec le Calvinisme."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5787a896-74d7-41b8-9bec-e63319b6b063",
                                                "sense_id": "68d8267d-e122-3abe-9ee4-73cb77a067b0",
                                                "text": "Le flinguer comme ça, de sang froid, sans être tout à fait de l’assassinat, y aurait quand même comme un cousinage !"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
